  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-research-lab",
      "text": "Research-lab toolkit for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai): a wiki-centric,\neval-rigor-driven research workflow distilled from **AutoSci** (wiki as the center of a research\nproject), **ASI-Bench** (evaluation rigor), **daily-arXiv-ai-enhanced** (digest),\n**ChatPaper** (paper review), **nature-skills / research-writing-skill** (academic writing),\n**Supervisor-Skills** (senior-review instinct), and hard lessons from real distillation\nexperiments (hypothesis → verdict loops, eval 口径 discipline)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools",
      "text": "| tool | purpose | inspired by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `rlab_wiki` | write wiki pages (`experiment/literature/decision/todo`) under `<project>/.rlab/wiki/` + rebuild index | AutoSci |\n| `rlab_experiment` | hypothesis → prediction → evidence → verdict → conclusion pages | AutoSci + falsifiability discipline |\n| `rlab_bench` | per-project eval ledger (`bench.jsonl`); flags 口径 (protocol) mismatches, e.g. mixing test/dev splits | ASI-Bench |\n| `rlab_paper_review` | arXiv id → adversarial 8-point review checklist (also applies to your own papers) | ChatPaper + ASI-Bench |\n| `rlab_arxiv_digest` | keyword digest of recent arXiv papers → `<project>/.rlab/digests/<date>.md` | daily-arXiv-ai-enhanced |\n| `rlab_writing` | line-anchored academic-expression check (passive/weak verbs/vague quantifiers/filler/term consistency) | nature-skills, research-writing-skill |\n| `rlab_related` | self-building keyword retrieval: NLP tokenization + SQLite FTS5, no preset lexicon — terms are TF-IDF-mined from your docs (EN words + ZH n-grams) and expanded iteratively (search → mine → merge → repeat) | hamuleite-style corpus, Rocchio relevance feedback |\n| `rlab_status` | one-screen project state: wiki counts, benc"
    },
    {
      "section": "On-disk layout",
      "text": "```\n<project>/.rlab/\n  wiki/\n    index.md            # auto-rebuilt\n    experiment/<id>.md  # hypothesis → verdict"
    },
    {
      "section": "Eval 口径 discipline (rlab_bench)",
      "text": "Every row must state `metric`, `split`, and for MTEB tasks the `hf_subset`. The report\nwarns whenever a task's history mixes splits — comparing test-vs-dev scores is the classic\nway papers fool themselves (and reviewers)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "from ~/.dsh/profiles/web",
      "text": "pnpm add @snow-the/dsh-research-lab@file:../.dsh-starter/plugins/dsh-research-lab"
    },
    {
      "section": "add \"dsh-research-lab\" to dsh.profile.bundles, then restart dsh web",
      "text": "```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Build",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm install && pnpm build   # tsc declarations + esbuild bundle → dist/\n```"
    }
  ],
